From 919244e86cbe3c000f79cc3c10907dd4ddb9a0a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:59:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Time capsule: towers that have come down stand until the year
 they did

The time capsule now also shows 14 towers of 150 m+ that were completed and
later demolished or destroyed (the original World Trade Center and 7 WTC,
the Singer Building, 270 Park Avenue, AXA Tower and others), each from its
completion year until the year it came down. They live in
src/lib/lostTowers.json with a source link each, and only appear while the
time capsule is on; today's map is unchanged.

- The dock counts the towers standing in the chosen year and says how many
  came down that year; a ghost ring marks where they stood, and their label
  says until when a lost tower stood.
- Clicking a lost tower opens its panel: when and how it came down, what
  replaced it, CTBUH and Wikipedia links. Its link opens the time capsule on
  a year it stood (/?year=1995&id=...).
- scripts/skyline-years.mjs counts lost towers while they stand and, from the
  year one came down, grows the city's extent again from the towers still
  standing, so the skyline extents follow the same rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015bnz9afFBBGLBukuAQtLqe
